SUMMARY:LIPF Presents: Alexander Kobrin
DESCRIPTION:“Van Cliburn of today” Alexander Kobrin returns to the Lancaster International Piano Festival for an evening of Beethoven\, Schubert and Brahms. Kobrin has received wide acclaim for his emotional\, technically inspired performances\, placing him at the forefront of today’s performing artists. He is an active guest soloist with the world’s leading orchestras\, including the New York Philharmonic\, Tokyo Philharmonic\, Orchestra Verdi\, Russian National Orchestra\, English Chamber Orchestra\, Orchestre de la Suisse Romande\, Royal Liverpool Philharmonic\, Dallas Symphony\, Berliner Symphony\, Swedish Radio Symphony\, Warsaw Philharmonic\, and the BBC Symphony Orchestra.“He surrendered neither the smoothness nor the dynamic fluidity that the modern piano allows\, and he gave his sense of fantasy free rein\, creating an almost confessional spirit .” — The New York Times  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n    Buy Tickets
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/lipf-presents-alexander-kobrin-2/
LOCATION:Barshinger Center at F&M College\, College Avenue\, Lancaster\, Pennsylvania\, 17603\, United States
